  "dependencies": [],
  "notes": "Cross-check implementation only; paper Falcon performance is from VecFalcon. This revision documents a 2026 best guess of future FIPS 206, not a published final standard. Compared with VecFalcon 61b326e: public keys are NTT encoded, encodings/hash-to-point are little-endian, signature infinity norm is capped at 840 instead of 2047, a 64-byte mu binds the hashed public key/context/message, secret keys include an additional 64-byte public-key hash, the base sampler uses 79 bits rather than 72, and SHAKE256x4 was removed. It is not a drop-in original round-3 Falcon implementation or interoperable wire format with the earlier VecFalcon API, despite the same public-key/signature lengths. Signatures remain padded 666/1280 bytes; exact unpadding parses the LSB-first compressed polynomial and checks against comp_decode. The scalar ref disables SIMD and uses software binary64, AVX2 uses native SIMD/FPU. Native degree-specific transcript KATs are mandatory for both. Public C API exposes only encoded keys; ExpandedSign is unavailable."
